# Thaumcraft Additions: Shock focus effect
effect.aqtweaks.stun=Stunned
focus.aqtweaks.shock.name=Shock
focus.aqtweaks.shock.text=Hurls a bolt of Potentia that jumps to nearby targets, further through water, and hits wet targets harder. Stuns what it strikes: they cannot attack or use items for a moment, longer with more duration. Creepers it hits become charged.
research.AQ_FOCUS_SHOCK.title=Focus Effect: Shock
research.AQ_FOCUS_SHOCK.stage.1=Air and water both carry a spark, yet the elemental foci only push, freeze or break. Raw Potentia, the stuff of motion itself, should be bolder than any of them. I will need to study it directly before I can bind it to a focus.
research.AQ_FOCUS_SHOCK.stage.2=A new focus effect. Shock throws a bolt of Potentia that stuns its target briefly, so it can neither strike nor use anything, and then arcs to up to two others nearby. Water carries the arc further, and a drenched target takes half again as much. Duration lengthens the stun; power scales the damage, much as frost does.
death.attack.aqtweaks_shock=%1$s was shocked by %2$s
death.attack.aqtweaks_shock.item=%1$s was shocked by %2$s using %3$s
death.attack.aqtweaks_shock_wild=%1$s was struck by stray lightning

# Thaumcraft Additions: Aegis focus effect
effect.aqtweaks.aegis_broken=Shield Broken
focus.aqtweaks.aegis.name=Aegis
focus.aqtweaks.aegis.text=Raises a shield of Praemunio in front of you for as long as you keep casting. It blocks hits from the front, spending a pool of damage that grows with power (5 per level, up to 25), and costs vis every second it is held. When the pool runs out the shield breaks, the hit that broke it is absorbed, and no focus containing Aegis can be cast for a few seconds. Lowering it early discards the pool.
research.AQ_FOCUS_AEGIS.title=Focus Effect: Aegis
research.AQ_FOCUS_AEGIS.stage.1=Healing mends a wound after it is made, and runic shielding wards only what a runic mind has woven into armour. Neither lets a caster simply stand against a blow. A pure Praemunio, drawn out and held steady, might. I will need to study it directly before I can bind it to a focus.
research.AQ_FOCUS_AEGIS.stage.2=A new focus effect. Aegis raises a shield of Praemunio in front of the caster while the focus is held. It stops anything that strikes from the front, spending a pool of damage set by its power, and runic glyphs on the shield fade as that pool is spent. It drinks vis steadily while it stands, and when it breaks Aegis cannot be cast again for a few seconds. It guards a single direction only; strike the caster from behind and it does nothing.

